7 true] [17592186423156 1075 #edb/ref 17592186423135 13194139534497 17592186045417 true] [17592186423156 1075 #edb/ref 17592186423136 13194139534497 17592186045417 true] [17592186423156 1075 #edb/ref 17592186423139 13194139534497 17592186045417 true] [17592186423156 1075 #edb/ref 17592186423143 13194139534497 17592186045417 true] [17592186423156 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139534497 17592186045417 true] [17592186423156 1077 "selection" 13194139534497 17592186045417 true] [17592186423156 1078 #edb/ref 17592186423139 13194139534497 17592186045417 true] [17592186423156 1079 #uuid "f6c7cc0f-00da-5a90-bc06-1408540bbde4" 13194139534497 17592186045417 true] [17592186423157 1068 #edb/ref 17592186423154 13194139534497 17592186045417 true] [17592186423157 1069 "q-128372" 13194139534497 17592186045417 true] [17592186423157 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534497 17592186045417 true] [17592186423157 1071 "Find a Cartesian equation of the plane that passes through the point $P(7,4,-3)$ and is perpendicular to the line \n$\\frac{x-3}{5}=\\frac{y-2}{4}=\\frac{z+1}{-2}.$" 13194139534497 17592186045417 true] [17592186423157 1072 #uuid "2a383fb4-f81d-5536-bfab-907adbefb459" 13194139534497 17592186045417 true] [17592186423157 1074 "First, we note that the position vector of $P$ is $p=⟨7,4,-3⟩.$ From the canonical equation, we find that the line is parallel to the vector $⟨5,4,-2⟩.$ So, the normal vector of the plane is \n\n$$\nn=⟨5,4,-2⟩.\n$$\n\nUsing the dot product, we can find the equation of the plane as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-p)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n & =p\\cdot n \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨5,4,-2⟩ & =⟨7,4,-3⟩\\cdot ⟨5,4,-2⟩ \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨5,4,-2⟩ & =57\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to obtain the Cartesian equation of the plane, we substitute $r=⟨x,y,z⟩$ into the equation above and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨x,y,z⟩\\cdot ⟨5,4,-2⟩ & =57 \\\\ 5x+4y-2z & =57 \\\\ 5x+4y-2z-57 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534497 17592186045417 true] [17592186423158 1068 #edb/ref 17592186423155 13194139534497 17592186045417 true] [17592186423158 1069 "q-332553" 13194139534497 17592186045417 true] [17592186423158 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139534497 17592186045417 true] [17592186423158 1071 "Consider the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-y=-{x}^{2}+5x-5.\n$$\n\nFind the general solution to this equation given that the complementary solution is ${y}_{c}(x)=A{e}^{x},$ where $A$ is an arbitrary constant." 13194139534497 17592186045417 true] [17592186423158 1072 #uuid "3e3fe7c4-ab73-58d1-aefb-b68674cbd3b7" 13194139534497 17592186045417 true] [17592186423158 1074 "To find the general solution of an inhomogeneous first-order linear equation, we must find the sum of the complementary and particular solutions.\n\nTo find the complementary solution ${y}_{c},$ we solve the corresponding homogeneous equation, given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{c}}{\\text{d}x}-{y}_{c}=0.\n$$\n\nSolving this equation, we find that the complementary solution is\n\n$$\n{y}_{c}=A{e}^{x}\n$$\n\nwhere $A$ is an arbitrary constant.\n\nWe now need to find the particular solution ${y}_{p}(x).$\n\nThe right-hand side of the inhomogeneous equation is a polynomial of degree $2.$ Therefore, we assume that the particular integral is also a polynomial of degree $2,$ i.e.,\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(x)=\\alpha {x}^{2}+\\beta x+\\gamma \n$$\n\nwhere $\\alpha ,$ $\\beta $, and $\\gamma $ are constants that are to be determined. \n\nCalculating the first derivative of ${y}_{p}$ gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{p}}{\\text{d}x}=2\\alpha x+\\beta .\n$$\n\nTo find the values of $\\alpha ,$ $\\beta ,$ and $\\gamma ,$  we substitute ${y}_{p}$ and ${y}_{p}^{′}$ into the differential equation:\n\n$$\n(2\\alpha x+\\beta )-(\\alpha {x}^{2}+\\beta x+\\gamma )=-{x}^{2}+5x-5\n$$\n\nWe then group the terms on the left-hand side, as follows:\n\n$$\n-\\alpha {x}^{2}+(2\\alpha -\\beta )x+(\\beta -\\gamma )=-{x}^{2}+5x-5\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients, we get the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\{\\begin{aligned}-\\alpha =-1\\, & (\\text{equating the coefficients of}\\,\\,{x}^{2}) \\\\ 2\\alpha -\\beta =5\\, & (\\text{equating the coefficients of}\\,\\,x) \\\\ \\beta -\\gamma =-5\\, & (\\text{equating the constants})\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving this system gives $\\alpha =1,\\beta =-3,\\gamma =2.$\n\nTherefore, the particular solution ${y}_{p}(x)$ is\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(x)={x}^{2}-3x+2.\n$$\n\nNow, since the general solution is given by\n\n$$\ny={y}_{c}+{y}_{p}\n$$\n\nthe general solution in our case is\n\n$$\ny=A{e}^{x}+{x}^{2}-3x+2.\n$$" 13194139534497 17592186045417 true] [17592186423159 1068 #edb/ref 17592186423156 13194139534497 17592186045417 true] [17592186423159 1069 "q-110933" 13194139534497 17592186045417 true] [17592186423159 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534497 17592186045417 true] [17592186423159 1071 "|  | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=1$ | $\\frac{1}{6}$ | $\\frac{1}{3}$ |\n| $X=2$ | $\\frac{1}{9}$ | $\\frac{1}{6}$ |\n| $X=3$ | $\\frac{1}{9}$ | $\\frac{1}{9}$ |\n\nCalculate $P(X=2,Y=2)$ given that the random variables $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ shown in the table above." 13194139534497 17592186045417 true] [17592186423159 1072 #uuid "451b002c-8ebd-53f3-82f6-93d93d564dd9" 13194139534497 17592186045417 true] [17592186423159 1074 "Using the table, we have\n\n$$\nP(X=2,Y=2)=f(2,2)=\\frac{1}{6}.\n$$" 13194139534497 17592186045417 true] [17592186423160 1068 #edb/ref 17592186423153 13194139534497 17592186045417 true] [17592186423160 1069 "q-140382" 13194139534497 17592186045417 true] [17592186423160 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139534497 17592186045417 true] [17592186423160 1071 "Given the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}1-\\text{i} & -1+3\\text{i} \\\\ 4\\text{i} & 3-8\\text{i}\\end{aligned}]$, find the result of applying to $A$ the following elementary row operation:\n\n$$\n{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-\\frac{4\\text{i}}{1-\\text{i}}){R}_{1}\n$$" 13194139534497 17592186045417 true] [17592186423160 1072 #uuid "a9bbaed4-c824-539a-9b36-056d32d45438" 13194139534497 17592186045417 true] [17592186423160 1074 "Let's apply the row operations to $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}1-\\text{i} & -1+3\\text{i} \\\\ 4\\text{i} & 3-8\\text{i}\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-\\frac{4\\text{i}}{1-\\text{i}}){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1-\\text{i} & -1+3\\text{i} \\\\ 4\\text{i}+(-\\frac{4\\text{i}(1-\\text{i})}{1-\\text{i}}) & 3-8\\text{i}+(-\\frac{4\\text{i}(-1+3\\text{i})}{1-\\text{i}})\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1-\\text{i} & -1+3\\text{i} \\\\ 4\\text{i}-4\\text{i} & \\frac{(3-8\\text{i})(1-\\text{i})+12+4\\text{i}}{1-\\text{i}}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1-\\text{i} & -1+3\\text{i} \\\\ 4\\text{i}-4\\text{i} & \\frac{7-7\\text{i}}{1-\\text{i}}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1-\\text{i} & -1+3\\text{i} \\\\ 0 & 7\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the result  is \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1-\\text{i} & -1+3\\text{i} \\\\ 0 & 7\\end{aligned}].\n$$" 13194139534497 17592186045417 true] [17592186423161 1058 #edb/ref 17592186423165 13194139534497 17592186045417 true] [17592186423161 1062 #uuid "0a6d729b-6546-5988-a8b2-ff1c871c9b65" 13194139534497 17592186045417 true] [17592186423161 1063 #edb/ref 17592186266018 13194139534497 17592186045417 true] [17592186423162 1058 #edb/ref 17592186423166 13194139534497 17592186045417 true] [17592186423162 1062 #uuid "19aea924-7038-5a67-94c0-4f850121cff5" 13194139534497 17592186045417 true] [17592186423162 1063 #edb/ref 17592186278186 13194139534497 17592186045417 true] [17592186423163 1058 #edb/ref 17592186423164 13194139534497 17592186045417 true] [17592186423163 1062 #uuid "5a85ef5f-8a7a-54b2-94f2-56cba543e4af" 13194139534497 17592186045417 true] [17592186423163 1063 #edb/ref 17592186364112 13194139534497 17592186045417 true] [17592186423164 1058 #edb/ref 17592186423167 13194139534497 17592186045417 true] [17592186423164 1062 #